# Speckit-Check - optional configuration.
#
# There is none. This file exists so the hook's folder matches every other
# shipped hook's shape, and so this note has somewhere to live.
#
# The hook reads three fixed things under the project root and nothing else:
#   .specify\                        does this project have planning infrastructure
#   .specify\memory\constitution.md  does it have its governing principles
#   specs\<feature>\spec.md|tasks.md which feature is newest, and is it finished
#
# KNOWN LIMITATION, deliberately not made configurable: a project that
# relocates its feature directory (Spec Kit honours an explicit
# SPECIFY_FEATURE_DIRECTORY) reads here as having no feature at all, so the
# hook names the full chain from speckit-specify. That fails toward suggesting
# a step the agent will find already done - a wasted sentence - rather than
# toward claiming finished work exists somewhere this hook never looked. An
# override would have to be set per project and would go stale silently, which
# is the worse failure for a hook that is meant to be quiet and right.
